# 6. CAPTURE EDITOR AND ANNOTATION

Build a practical image-editing workspace.

## 6.1 Basic Editing

Include:

- Crop
- Resize
- Rotate
- Flip horizontally and vertically
- Undo and redo
- Zoom in and out
- Fit to window
- Actual-size view
- Copy image to clipboard
- Save
- Save As
- Export to another supported format

Preserve the original capture until the user explicitly overwrites or replaces it.

## 6.2 Annotation Tools

Include:

- Arrow
- Line
- Rectangle
- Ellipse
- Freehand drawing
- Text
- Numbered markers
- Highlight
- Blur or pixelate
- Fill and outline colours
- Stroke thickness
- Font size
- Undo and redo

Annotation objects should be editable before final export where practical.

Blur and pixelation must be applied to the exported image itself, not merely represented by a transparent overlay.

## 6.3 Clipboard and Drag-and-Drop

Support, where practical:

- Copy image
- Paste image from clipboard
- Open an image by dragging it into the editor
- Drag an exported image into supported applications
- Copy OCR text
- Copy selected annotation content where applicable

Display useful error messages for unsupported clipboard formats.

## 6.4 Pin to Screen

Implement a real floating image window that can remain above other windows.

Requirements:

- Pin a captured image to the desktop.
- Keep it above other windows when requested.
- Allow moving and resizing.
- Provide zoom controls.
- Support multiple pinned images if practical.
- Provide a close button.
- Allow the user to unpin or hide an image.
- Avoid stealing keyboard focus unnecessarily.
- Clean up pinned windows when the application exits.

Use a native desktop window or supported framework capability. A normal HTML element inside the main window does not satisfy this requirement.

