# 7. SCREEN RECORDER

Implement actual screen recording using supported desktop capture APIs.

## 7.1 Recording Modes

Provide:

- Full display recording
- Selected region recording where supported
- Monitor selection
- Optional microphone input
- Optional system audio when supported
- Optional webcam overlay only if properly implemented

Display a clear recording indicator and elapsed time.

## 7.2 Recording Controls

Include:

- Start
- Pause and resume, if supported
- Stop
- Cancel
- Elapsed time
- Output location
- Recording status

Prevent accidental termination or silent loss of an active recording.

## 7.3 Recording Settings

Allow the user to configure supported options:

- Frame rate
- Resolution
- Video format
- Audio input
- Microphone volume
- System audio
- Output folder
- Filename template

Expose only settings that the recording backend actually supports.

## 7.4 Audio Handling

- List available microphone devices where supported.
- Let users select an input device.
- Clearly indicate whether audio capture is active.
- Handle permission failures.
- Handle unavailable or disconnected devices.
- Do not claim system audio recording works if the selected backend cannot capture it.

## 7.5 Video Processing

Where supported, include:

- Trim start and end
- Extract audio from video
- Export audio to MP3 when the required encoder is available and properly licensed
- Convert video formats where implemented
- Show real progress for long-running operations
- Allow cancellation
- Preserve the original file by default

Use a suitable media-processing backend, such as FFmpeg, only after reviewing packaging, licensing, binary size, security, and redistribution requirements.

Do not bundle every codec or binary unnecessarily.

