# 19. ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The application is ready for release only when:

- The main window is compact and usable.
- The system tray is real and reliable.
- Close-to-tray works as configured.
- The user can quit the application completely.
- Supported capture modes work.
- Saving and exporting create valid files.
- Annotation and Undo/Redo work.
- Recording produces playable output.
- Audio controls accurately reflect backend support.
- OCR produces actual text when supported.
- Pinned images remain in independent floating windows.
- Global hotkeys register and work correctly.
- Settings persist between launches.
- The application remains responsive during long operations.
- Idle resource usage has been measured.
- Installer size has been measured.
- Security-sensitive operations are appropriately restricted.
- No major workflow depends on fake buttons or placeholder logic.
- The production build and packaging process complete successfully.

Features that cannot be implemented reliably must be clearly documented rather than falsely marked complete.

