When implementation work is complete, provide:

1. Project audit summary.
2. Features that were already working.
3. Features newly implemented.
4. Files added, removed, or modified.
5. Dependencies added or removed and the reasons.
6. Desktop framework decision and justification.
7. Build and test commands executed.
8. Actual test results.
9. Original versus final installer size.
10. Original versus final startup time and idle RAM usage, if measured.
11. Known limitations.
12. Features requiring additional native APIs or optional dependencies.
13. Exact instructions to build, package, install, and run the application.

Do not claim full completion if any required feature remains incomplete.

## FINAL DEVELOPMENT RULE

First audit the actual repository and create the implementation plan. Then implement the highest-priority features in small, testable stages.

Prioritize a compact interface, a reliable system tray, fast startup, low idle resource usage, real screenshot capture, and stable recording.

Keep the application lightweight without sacrificing reliability or security. Preserve working features, avoid unnecessary rewrites, and verify every feature before marking it complete.
